--- raw_data/ccbiblestudy_CT_joshua_21.txt
130: 〔文意註解〕「亞因和屬城的郊野、淤他和屬城的郊野、伯示麥和屬城的郊野」：『亞因』位於別是巴西北方約6公里，迦薩東南方約40公里，原屬西緬支派(參書十九7)；『伯示麥』不同於書十五10的「伯示麥」，位於伯善北方約20公里，耶斯列東南方約22公里，原屬西緬支派(參書十九22)。
--- raw_data/ccbiblestudy_GT_joshua_21.txt
143: 「亞拿突」：為先知耶利米之故鄉(耶1：1)，在耶路撒冷以北約五公里(三英里)。
147: 「亞拿突」(18節)是先知耶利米的出生地(耶一1)。──
--- raw_data/biblehub_study_joshua_21.txt
437: These towns belonged to the inheritance assigned to the descendants of Aaron, the priestly line within the Levites. Juttah lay in Judah’s hill country near Hebron, while Beth-shemesh, meaning “house of the sun,” stood in the western lowlands and later received the ark when the Philistines returned it to Israel (1 Samuel 6:12–15). God placed priestly families among the tribes so that worship, instruction, and sacrificial service would remain near the people.
504: Anathoth was a Levitical city allocated to the descendants of Aaron, the priestly line, within the tribe of Benjamin. It is significant in biblical history as the hometown of the prophet Jeremiah (Jeremiah 1:1). The city is mentioned in various contexts, including as a place of refuge and a site of prophetic activity. Anathoth’s association with the priestly class underscores its religious importance. Archaeologically, it is identified with the modern village of Anata, located northeast of Jerusalem. The city’s role in biblical prophecy and its connection to Jeremiah highlight its spiritual significance.
--- raw_scripture/約書亞記/第19章.txt
1: 為西緬支派的人，按著宗族，拈出第二鬮。他們所得的地業是在猶大人地業中間。
7: 又有亞因、利門、以帖、亞珊，共四座城，還有屬城的村莊；
17: 為以薩迦人，按著宗族，拈出第四鬮。
22: 又達到他泊、沙哈洗瑪、伯示麥，直通到約但河為止，共十六座城，還有屬城的村莊。

